A||||6||Green Meanie||Suggested Fiero performance magazines?
Z||000000||Green Meanie||07-15-99||10:25 AM||||Hey everyone!  <p>I'm a new owner of a 85 Fiero GT.  I want to <br>kind of do it up a bit, not just engine wise<br>but looks wise aswell on the outside and in.<p>can anyone suggest any good magazines that I could start subscribing to?<p>Thanks,<p>Chris
Z||000001||vurbanson||07-15-99||04:57 PM||||You should try the FIERO magazine. It's a quarterly magazine (I believe) turned out by Fiero Owners Club Of America.  There's a site on the net and you can subscribe right away.  Kit Car magazine has a fair bit of stuff on the Fiero also.
Z||000002||batboy||07-15-99||05:08 PM||||Just ask the guys here in the Forum what you want to know. Some of the pictures I've seen of some of these guy's Fieros are awesome. Plenty of Fiero site out there on the internet, just surf away. I'm doing a bunch of neat stuff to my Fiero mainly from suggestions or ideas that I've picked up here in this Forum. Take a before and after photo, then show them to us after you get your Fiero done. Good luck.
Z||000003||RICK||07-15-99||05:08 PM||||Has anybody ordered the back issues that they sell?  How many are there?
Z||000004||Pretender||07-16-99||12:33 AM||||i've bought some hi-po pontiac back issues and found them to be worth the money., but i was only able to get 2 of them. the rest were sold out at the time..
Z||000005||Carrolles||07-16-99||06:48 AM||||When I joined FOCOA in 97 I ordered all of the back issues of Fiero Owner Magazine.  It cost around $60.00.  I thoroughly enjoyed reading them cover to cover from issue one to see the evolution of the car and the clubs.<p>A few of the very early issues are actually Xerox copies since the originals are all gone but in those days the magazine was more like a newsletter than a magazine anyway.<p>I feel like it was well worth the money.<p>You might also try the Fiero Owners Association.  They also have a quarterly magazine.<p>Welcome to the world of Fieros.<p>Carroll
Z||000006||ChadMan||07-16-99||08:06 AM||||Kit Car magazine sometimes has good Fiero info, but not often enough to warrant subscribing.  I check it out every month at the newsstand, and if there's Fiero info, I buy it.  John Norman's "Obsession" (Northstar w/nitrous) was featured in there one month, as was Ed Shipp's 88 GT with supercharged 3800 and PISA ZR-2 body kit.  They even ran a Fiero engine swap guide one month written by FOCOA's "Fiero Doc."
